    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e28a2b8_a0b12e18",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/SharedContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T17:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should not be public as initialization should only happen once in a controlled manner.  Whether or not to instantiate the capture manager could be a constructor argument to SharedContext (or it could take the sk_sp/std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCaptureManager\u003e directly so that the Context factory can create it however it wants to).  This would unfortunately require updating all of the subclasses of SharedContext to pass it through.\n\nSince there is already an out-of-band initialization step for SharedContext (setRendererProvider), I\u0027d vote to remove `initCaptureManager()` and have a private `setCaptureManager()` that is called in `Context()`, as it\u0027s already a friend.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "62d076f35abf6cc31f0b515a51f02bf070910912",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6d86c27_5621f53a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/SharedContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 11964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T15:25:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Since there was no need to create it out of band, I kept the new private `setCaptureManager` call in the constructor.",
      "parentUuid": "3e28a2b8_a0b12e18",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "62d076f35abf6cc31f0b515a51f02bf070910912",
