    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3872dbd_cf6777cb",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/SharedContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T17:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia naming convention is that `captureManager()` would return `SkCaptureManager*` and `refCaptureManager()` would return `sk_sp\u003cSkCaptureManager\u003e`.\n\nIn this case, the SharedContext owns the SkCaptureManager so it technically never has to let other people ref it (the SharedContext in graphite is the last object to be deleted on teardown).  It should just return `SkCaptureManager*`.\n\nGiven that, SkCaptureManager doesn\u0027t necessarily have to extend SkRefCnt, we could always have the context owners use `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCaptureManager\u003e` instead, but that might not be possible with Ganesh or the CPU context\u0027s life times so sk_sp is also fine for now.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "62d076f35abf6cc31f0b515a51f02bf070910912",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
